        "problem": "Find $Zx$ if \n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1+(-7)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$Zx=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].$",
